              "notes": "Chrome alum, KCr(SO4)2*12H2O. The report equates the label with chrome alum from peer-reviewed literature and gives CAS RN 7788-99-0 from a chemical reference. No ontology term covers the potassium double salt or its dodecahydrate; CHEBI:53471 chromium(III) sulfate is the nearest parent, lacking both the potassium and the twelve waters."
            },
            {
              "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
              "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
              "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:53471 ('chromium(III) sulfate') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
            }
          ]
        }
