          },
          {
            "timestamp": "2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00",
            "curator": "edison_literature_identity",
            "action": "ANNOTATED",
            "changes": "Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/Poly-beta-hydroxyalkanoate-edison-literature.md (local artifact — research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather than linked). Report verdict: **Recommended interpretation:** a legacy name for the **polyhydroxyalkanoate (PHA) polymer family**, not a single chemical, salt, hydrate, buffer, extract, commercial formulation, or defined culture-medium mixture. PHAs are microbial polyesters containing hydroxyalkanoate repeat units and encompass chemically distinct homopolymers, random or block copolymers, and terpolymers. Their monomer composi No ontology CURIE was proposed. Recorded as provenance only — no grounding applied from this run. Edison's recommendations are deliberately conservative, and a plausible identifier promoted by a mechanism that never decided anything is what #203 and #263 exist to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator's to accept or reject.",
            "llm_assisted": true
          },
          {
            "timestamp": "2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00",
            "curator": "decompose_py_media_and_ground_categories",
            "action": "GROUNDED_TO_CHEBI_CLASS",
            "previous_status": "NEEDS_EXPERT",
            "new_status": "MAPPED",
            "changes": "UNMAPPED_0836 -> CHEBI:78037; ontology_id CHEBI:78037 (SYNONYM_MATCH). Grounded to the ChEBI class CHEBI:78037 ('polyhydroxyalkanoate'): poly-beta-hydroxyalkanoate and polyhydroxyalkanoate are the same polymer class under two spellings — the beta- records the 3-hydroxy position that PHA implies — so this is a naming variant, not a subclass relation, and needs no registry mint.",
            "llm_assisted": false
          },
          {
            "timestamp": "2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00",
            "curator": "move_mapped_out_of_unmapped_collection",
            "action": "MOVED_TO_MAPPED_COLLECTION",
            "changes": "Moved from unmapped_ingredients.yaml to mapped_ingredients.yaml (#370). The record was already MAPPED; it had been promoted in place by a path that does not move between collections, and reconcile_sssom reads only the mapped collection — so its mapping was curated but unpublished.",
            "llm_assisted": false
          },
          {
            "timestamp": "2026-09-02T17:40:44.716277+00:00",
